// 63b CONTROL — the same file shape with a COMPARISON guard instead of a call.
//
// Without this, "the guard probe was refused" is equally well explained by the
// probe file being malformed, by --src-root being wrong, or by two clauses over
// `int` failing exhaustiveness. This file differs from `GuardProbe` in exactly
// one respect: the guard is `u == 1` rather than `IsAdmin(u) == :yes`.
//
// It must COMPILE. If it does not, 63b measured nothing.
module GuardControl

public atom IsAdmin(int u)
IsAdmin(1) -> :yes
IsAdmin(_) -> :no

public atom Check(int u)
Check(u) when u == 1 -> :admin
Check(_)             -> :ordinary
